WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.882
Texture.

2
00:00:01.042 --> 00:00:03.782
Texture is how something feels when you touch it.

3
00:00:03.942 --> 00:00:05.289
Tree bark is rough.

4
00:00:05.449 --> 00:00:06.842
Glass is smooth.

5
00:00:07.002 --> 00:00:08.210
Wool is soft.

6
00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.716
Bubble wrap is bumpy.

7
00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.409
A sponge is squashy.

8
00:00:11.569 --> 00:00:12.869
A stone is hard.

9
00:00:13.029 --> 00:00:16.094
Artists notice texture with their hands, not just their eyes.

10
00:00:16.794 --> 00:00:18.234
Recording a texture.

11
00:00:18.394 --> 00:00:20.484
You can record a texture with a rubbing.

12
00:00:20.644 --> 00:00:24.916
Put thin paper over something bumpy and rub the side of a crayon over it, gently.

13
00:00:25.076 --> 00:00:26.377
The bumps come through.

14
00:00:26.537 --> 00:00:28.162
The texture draws itself.

15
00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.255
Changing the paint.

16
00:00:30.415 --> 00:00:32.226
Paint does not have to be smooth.

17
00:00:32.386 --> 00:00:34.615
Stir rice into it and it goes bumpy.

18
00:00:34.775 --> 00:00:36.215
Flour makes it thick.

19
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:37.768
Sugar makes it gritty.

20
00:00:37.928 --> 00:00:39.229
Water makes it runny.

21
00:00:39.389 --> 00:00:42.454
Guess first, then add it, then look at what really happened.

22
00:00:43.154 --> 00:00:44.640
Choosing a material.

23
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.608
When you make a picture, choose materials that feel like the thing.

24
00:00:48.768 --> 00:00:50.904
Sandpaper for a rough tree trunk.

25
00:00:51.064 --> 00:00:53.107
Cotton wool for a fluffy cloud.

26
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.661
Foil for a shiny fish.

27
00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.632
That is choosing for a purpose.
